  "schema_version": 1,
  "kind": "help-article",
  "title": "Supported Data Stores, File Types, and Regions",
  "source": {
    "url": "https://help.zscaler.com/dspm/supported-data-stores-file-types-and-regions",
    "node": "1498686",
    "revision": "3233351",
    "updated": "2026-09-09",
    "updated_basis": "pdf-last-modified"
  },
  "captured_at": "2026-10-19",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "text": "DSPM supports the scanning of AWS, Azure, GCP data stores (storage services, virtual machines, and their associated disks and databases), and on-premises databases for sensitive data, vulnerabilities, and misconfigurations. This article outlines the support level for both managed and unmanaged data stores, specific capabilities regarding posture management, data classification (DLP), scan methods, and authentication mechanisms. To learn more, see About Scan Settings."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Key Concepts",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "text": "The following terms are used to define the scope of DSPM's capabilities:"
    },
    {
      "item": "Onboarding Types: The following models can be onboarded:",
      "depth": 0,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          16
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "AWS: Organization or Standalone Account",
      "depth": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          3
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Azure: Tenant or Management Group",
      "depth": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          5
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "GCP: Organization",
      "depth": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          3
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Posture Labels: Labels describe the security and configuration checks performed on the data store:",
      "depth": 0,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          14
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Public Exposure: Indicates the resource is accessible from the public internet.",
      "depth": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          15
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Encryption: The type of encryption (customer‑managed key or platform‑managed key) applied to the resource.",
      "depth": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          10
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Logging: Confirms access logs and audit trails are enabled.",
      "depth": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          7
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Backup Recovery: Checks backup and retention policies.",
      "depth": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          15
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Access Control: Validates IAM policies and ACL configurations.",
      "depth": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          14
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Guardrails: Indicates that guardrails are enabled for an AI service.",
      "depth": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          10
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Has AI/ML Package: Checks if AI or ML packages are installed on a compute instance.",
      "depth": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          17
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Has AI/ML Model: Checks if AI or ML models are present on a compute instance.",
      "depth": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          15
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Data Classification:",
      "depth": 0,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          20
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Data is classified with Zscaler's DLP engines and dictionaries. Data classification is performed via full, incremental, historical, or sampling scans.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "Authentication Mechanisms: The following methods are used for authentication and to establish trust to perform data scans:",
      "depth": 0,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          25
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Cloud Native: Cross‑account IAM roles (AWS), service principals or managed identities (Azure), or service accounts (GCP).",
      "depth": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          12
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Bring Your Own Identity:",
      "depth": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          23
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Credential-Based: Requires username or password or access keys stored in the vault. This is mostly required for unmanaged databases.",
      "depth": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          16
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Certificate-Based: Mutual TLS (mTLS) authentication.",
      "depth": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          17
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Supported Data Stores",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "text": "The scan types, security postures, authentication types, malware and vulnerability scanning, etc., along with regions supported for the following data stores and services are listed:"
    },
    {
      "item": "Managed Data Stores",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "Onboarding Mode: DSPM provides support for default and custom onboarding of all three cloud service provider accounts.",
